  🛠️ **Fix Cloudflare Error 521:**


  **Cause: SSL/TLS Mismatch**

  Your server serves HTTP (port 80), but Cloudflare might be trying HTTPS.

  **Solution: Update Cloudflare SSL Settings**

  1. Go to Cloudflare Dashboard
    • Select your domain: otk-help.martinmeer.com
    • Go to SSL/TLS tab
  2. Change SSL/TLS Mode:
    • Current setting is probably: Full or Full (Strict)
    • Change to: Flexible


     Flexible = Cloudflare (HTTPS) → Your Server (HTTP)

  3. Wait 1-2 minutes for changes to propagate
  4. Test again:


     curl https://otk-help.martinmeer.com/actuator/health

  ---

  📋 **Cloudflare SSL/TLS Modes Explained:**

  | Mode | Cloudflare → Server | When to Use |
  |------|---------------------|-------------|
  | Off | HTTP → HTTP | Never (insecure) |
  | Flexible ✅ | HTTPS → HTTP | Your setup (no SSL on server) |
  | Full | HTTPS → HTTPS (self-signed OK) | Server has SSL cert |
  | Full (Strict) | HTTPS → HTTPS (valid cert only) | Server has valid SSL cert |
  You need: Flexible because your nginx listens on HTTP only (port 80).
  ---

